If you look at the source code, this is what you'll find:

boolean
monnear(mon, x, y)
register struct monst *mon;
register int x,y;
/* Is the square close enough for the monster to move or attack into? */
{
	register int distance = dist2(mon->mx, mon->my, x, y);
	if (distance==2 && mon->data==&mons[PM_GRID_BUG]) return 0;
	return((boolean)(distance < 3));
}

keepdogs() calls monnear() to decide whether the pet can follow
you down the stairs, and monnear has a special case for grid bugs.
I would guess that the case wasn't added specifically because of
the implications of pet grid bugs, but as it is it does the Right
Thing.

